T|                  FADE IN:                                                            
O|
S|                 EXT. LAKE HOUSE - SUNSET                             1              
O|
N|                  The sky is a shimmering expanse of stars, packed together.          
O|
C,E|                                   LOUISE (V.0O.)                                    
U|                          Memory is a strange thing.                                 
O|
S|                 EXT. LAKE HOUSE -— SUNSET                            2              
O|
N|                  A modern home built on the shore with a large deck.                 
N|                  The skin of the lake is a cloudy mirror.                            
N,I|                  LOUISE BANKS stares up at the sky, leaning against the deck’s       
N|                  railing. Merlot glass in one hand.                                  
O|
N,I|                  Louise has a clean, timeless look about her; the kind of            
N,I|                  woman who ages gracefully. Short hair.                              
C,E|                                   LOUISE (V.O.)                                     
U|                          It doesn’t work like I thought it                          
U|                          did. We are so bound by time; by                           
U|                          its order.                                                 
O|
N|                  She steps back inside, a little tipsy, smiling.                     
O|
S|          A2     INT. LAKE HOUSE -— CONTINUOUS                       A2              
O|
N|                  Stacks of books on shelves and tables. A telescope against a        
N|                  glass wall. And dry-erase boards, marked with foreign               
N|                  languages. Different colors for different dialects.                 
C,E|                                   LOUISE (V.O.)                                     
U|                          Maybe there’s a higher order.                              
O|
N|                  Mingled here are also dinner plates. Candlelight.                   
O|
C|                                   LOUISE                                            
U|                          Darling, is there any more wine?                           
N|                  She pauses when a deck light winks on outside. Her eyes             
N|                  sparkle when she sees something:                                    
O|
N|                  A question, written on the glass, lit from outdoors.                
N|                 “Do you want to make a baby?”                                       
O|
C,E|                                   LOUISE (V.O.)                                     
U|                          I used to think this was the                               
U|                          beginning of your story.                                   
O|
O|
O|                                  Blue Draft (05/06/2015)           2.               
O|
N|                  Louise goes right to the glass, wanting to touch the question       
N|                  with her finger to make sure it’s real.                             
O|
N,G|                  CLOSE ON HER FACE: From outside looking in, a curious               
N|                  circular shadow is thrown from the deck light. But her eyes         
N|                  start to water.                                                     
N,G|                  In the background, the bedroom door hangs open and the              
N|                  silhouette of a MAN leans against the frame, watching her.          
O|
N|                  Louise turns around, smiling again. We know her answer.             
O|
S|                 INT. MERCY HILL GENERAL HOSPITAL ~— MORNING          3              
N,I|                  Louise cradles a NEWBORN GIRL in her arms. Her name: HANNAH.        
O|
N|                  Hannah reaches up.                                                  
N|                  Crooks her tiny hand around Louise’s finger.                        
O|
N|                  LATER                                                               
N|                 A NURSE starts to take baby Hannah to give Louise some rest.         
N|                  Hannah BLEATS and reaches for her mother.                           
O|
N|                  Louise smiles through the exhaustion and pulls her back--           
O|
C|                                   LOUISE                                            
U|                          Okay, come back, come back to me...                        
O|
S|                 EXT. LAKE HOUSE YARD — AFTERNOON                      4              
O|
N|                 Four-year-old HANNAH dressed as a cowgirl.                           
N|                 On a toy riding horse with wheels for hooves.                        
N|                 Giggling like she can’t stop.                                        
C,E|                                   LOUISE (V.O.)                                     
U|                          I remember moments in the middle.                          
O|
N|                 She pulls both finger-guns, aimed at us.                             
C|                                   HANNAH                                            
U|                          Stick ‘em up!                                              
O|
S|                 INT. HANNAH’S ROOM — NIGHT                           5              
O|
N|                 BHight-year-old Hannah is tucked in bed.                             
N|                 Said to us as a prayer:                                              
C|                                   HANNAH                                            
U|                          I love you.                                                
O|
O|
O|                                  Blue Draft (05/06/2015)           3.              
O|
S|                 INT. LAKE HOUSE - NIGHT                                            
N|                  Twelve-year-old Hannah glowers at us:                              
O|
C|                                   HANNAH                                           
U|                          tT hate you!                                              
O|
N|                 -~-and storms into her room.                                       
O|
S|                 INT. MERCY HILL GENERAL HOSPITAL - MORNING                         
O|
N|                  Twelve-year-old daughter HANNAH lies, eyes closed.                 
O|
N|                  Hannah is pale. Her head has been shaved in the last month.        
C,E|                                   LOUISE (V.O.)                                    
U|                          And this was the end.                                     
O|
N|                  Louise holds her daughter’s hand in hers.                          
N|                  Her thumb traces Hannah’s knuckles.                                
N|                  A life monitor beeps as Hannah’s heart stops.                      
O|
N|                  Hannah’s eyes roll up and she sighs her final breath.              
O|
N|                  Louise’s grip on her daughter tightens. Trembling.                 
O|
N|                  A Nurse starts to pull Louise away, but she hangs on-- now         
N|                  it’s mother trying to return to her baby girl--                    
C|                                   LOUISE                                           
U|                          Come back-- come back to me, baby--                       
O|
N|                  Louise is unaware she’s crying. Hannah remains motionless.         
O|
C,E|                                   LOUISE (V.O.)                                    
U|                          But now I’m not so sure I believe                         
U|                          in beginnings and endings. There                          
U|                          are days that define your story                           
U|                          beyond your life.                                         
T|                                                         CUT TO BLACK.              
C,E|                                   LOUISE (V.0O.)                                   
U|                          Like the day they arrived.                                
